course: dictionary
lesson: 2253
title: Craters: holes from impacts and volcanoes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crater is a large, bowl-shaped hole in the ground. Two things make craters: something very heavy crashing into the ground, like a meteorite, or the hollow at the top of a volcano. Look at the clues in this sentence: «About 66 million years ago an asteroid roughly 10 kilometres wide hit what is now the Yucatan coast of Mexico, making the Chicxulub crater about 180 kilometres across.» The asteroid hit the ground, and the crater is a huge hole, so crater must mean a hole made by a hit.
explain: Now test your meaning. «Water ice exists in permanently shadowed craters near the Moon's poles.» If you swap in hole, it reads: water ice exists in permanently shadowed holes near the Moon's poles. That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Shadowed tells you the sun never reaches the bottom of the hollow.
explain: There are two kinds of crater. An impact crater is made when a rock from space hits a surface. A volcanic crater is the hollow at the top of a volcano, as in «lakes form in craters of old volcanoes». Both are bowl-shaped holes, but they start in different ways.
fact: A crater is a large, bowl-shaped hole in the ground.
fact: An impact crater is made when something heavy, such as a meteorite, hits the ground.
fact: A volcanic crater is the hollow at the top of a volcano.
fact: The Chicxulub crater in Mexico is about 180 kilometres across.
fact: Children can model craters on the Moon by dropping marbles into flour.
exercise: «The Chicxulub crater is about 180 kilometres across.» What does across mean here? | Up and down | Under the ground | Round and round | *From one side to the other
exercise: «Lakes form in craters of old volcanoes.» Where is a volcanic crater? | At the bottom of a river | In the middle of a cloud | Under the sea floor | *At the top of a volcano
exercise: «Water ice exists in permanently shadowed craters near the Moon's poles.» What does shadowed suggest about a crater? | It is full of water | It is very hot | *Sunlight never reaches it | It is on Earth
test: Which thing makes a crater? | A bird landing on a branch | A river flowing slowly | *A meteorite crashing into the ground | Snow falling gently
test: Ayla says a crater is a tall mountain. What is the right meaning? | *A bowl-shaped hole | A river bend | A tall mountain | A flat plain
exam: The Moon has many craters. What made most of them? | Rain washing away the soil | People digging for gold | Strong winds blowing sand | *Rocks from space hitting it
